# Design: V0.8.1 A4 print-and-play kit

## Problem
V0.8 must reach real families for playtests, but the only
artifacts were the web build and a V0.6.2 CSS print pack for a
different board. The kit had to print on one basic
black-and-white A4 printer with no color, no paid services, and
zero drift from the released rules.

## Approach
One generator (tools/make_a4_print_kit.py) derives everything
from rules_v08_succession.json via reportlab vector drawing.
The board is a single 584 x 410 mm artwork tiled 2x2; every
position is recorded in print/kit-manifest.json and cross-checked
by tests. A 13-value guard in main() stops generation if the
rules JSON no longer matches the numbers the prose prints.

## Key trade-offs
- Butt-join over lap-join: families cut every tile on BOTH dashed
  lines and tape straight edges from the back. Lap-join saved
  artwork duplication but forced per-tile furniture that collided
  with the title and duplicated at the joins.
- Overlap 10 mm (spec 8-10): gates sit just north of the
  horizontal cut; 10 mm keeps every gate ring >= 6 mm from its
  keeper page edge (9 mm left the east gate 0.15 mm short).
- PERISTYLE label above the octagon: below it, the text top sat
  0.4 mm from the cut line and a wandering cut would shave it.
- Registration crosses at x=40/560 share x across the cut so
  taping stacks them; the decumanus row (7.1 mm corridors)
  cannot host a 9.6 mm crosshair anywhere.
- Symbols distinguish by shape, not gray: open circles, double
  circles, arch-in-ring gates, octagon Peristyle, stars with 4+.
  The only grayscale (district letters) got white knockout
  plates so cheap printers keep them crisp.
- Verification is numeric first: /tmp audit recomputes every
  drawn bbox (labels vs circles, cut clearance, safe zones, reg
  marks vs circles) because the vision analyzer misreports
  positions; renders then confirm joins and threshold survival.

## Gotchas
- pdftoppm prefix quirk: prefix "foo" yields foo-1.png, not
  <pdfname>-1.png.
- Analyzer text claims can hallucinate wholesale ("v0.6.3",
  "De Prochylo's manureing"); verify quotes with pdftotext
  before acting.
- Physical assembly is UNVERIFIED: no printer on this machine.
  Digital stitch, threshold simulation, and geometry checks only.

